  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Output/s</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output/s as listed by the project staff.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: COVID-19 vaccines delivered. 
Indicator: By 2024, the number of required COVID-19 vaccine doses for vaccinating at least 4 million people delivered to the central epidemiology unit and the Regional Medical Supplies Divisions 
Achievement: 7.125 
Progress/Status: 1a) 7.125 million people fully vaccinated from 15 million doses delivered to Central EPI stores and Regional stores under ADB financing.

Approved contracts for procurement of 15 million doses of Sinopharm Vaccines amounting to $105 million. 
Data Source: Epidemiology Unit</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="4"></target>
     <actual value="7.125"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Capacity of vaccine transport systems expanded 
Indicator: By 2022, 36 refrigerated trucks delivered to transport vaccines 
Progress/Status: 3a) Deprioritized. Government used existing resources to
transport vaccines. 
Data Source: Epidemiology Unit, medical supplies division data 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="36"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Capacity of vaccine transport systems expanded 
Indicator: By 2023, at least 25 district-specific vehicle hire contracts signed for dedicated transport to enable vulnerable women and people with disabilities to access vaccination centers in all nine provinces 
Progress/Status: 3c) No longer required.
The government used available vehicles for vaccine and staff movement and this was not required because the campaign was carried out in a staggered manner area by area and was not made viable across the full country at 2000 centers as envisaged in the NDVP. This had to be rolled out in this manner as vaccine arrival was staggered. 
Data Source: Health Promotion Bureau and quarterly progress reports 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="25"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Capacity of vaccine transport systems expanded 
Indicator: By 2023, mobile communication teams (50% women) in at least 50% of medical officers of health areas reporting increased knowledge of gender and socially sensitive ways of communicating COVID-19 vaccine benefits and risks to women and excluded and vulnerable groups 
Progress/Status: 3b) This activity (a survey) was not carried out and as the COVD-19 vaccination is now completed and as 82% of the eligible population is now vaccinated this activity can be repurposed. 

According to Health Promotion Bureau (HPB), UNICEF/World Bank supported formative surveys have confirmed that these groups were reached. 
Data Source: Health Promotion Bureau and quarterly progress reports 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="50"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3  Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Vaccination information dissemination and monitoring systems strengthened. 
Indicator: By 2023, at least 90% of the 5,000 participants (60% women) of information campaigns assisted in COVID-19 vaccination in the respective medical officer of health areas 
Achievement: 100 
Progress/Status: 2c) More than 5000 participants assisted via mothers-support clubs, of which 90% are women. Activities were supported by other donor and government funds. 
Data Source: Health Promotion Bureau and quarterly progress reports</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="90"></target>
     <actual value="100"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Vaccine-related medical waste management strengthened 
Indicator: By 2024, 12 satellite hospitals provide clustered HCWM practices 
Progress/Status: 4a) Due to changed plan and priority of DGHS,
this output was deprioritized and will no longer be
pursued. 
Data Source: Quarterly progress reports 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="12"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Vaccine-related medical waste management strengthened 
Indicator: By 2024, sewerage waste disposal improved in 26 COVID-19 managed hospitals 
Progress/Status: 4b) No longer a prioritized need. When the economic situation improves, government may consider requesting additional resources from ADB or other donors. 
Data Source: Quarterly progress reports 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="26"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Vaccination information dissemination and monitoring systems strengthened. 
Indicator: By 2024, an electronic immunization data management system established and integrated in the national health information system with sex- and age-disaggregated data. 
Achievement: N 
Progress/Status: 2a) Functional; Financed from other donor and GOSL funds. The electronic immunization data management system is available with age disaggregated data. 
Data Source: Health Information Unit and the Epidemiology Unit with technical guidance from WHO Sri Lanka 
Baseline year: 2021 
